[12.326378, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.376311, "o", "[HIGH  ] M14-01 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.2)\u001b[m\u001b[K the runtimeSessionId comes from the browser: AgentCore does not enforce session-to-user mappings, so a replayed ID lands in someone else's microVM\r\n[HIGH  ] M14-02 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.2)\u001b[m\u001b[K tsg-web-frontend (end-user reachable) may call InvokeAgentRuntime, InvokeAgentRuntimeCommand, InvokeAgentRuntimeCommandShell on the runtime: InvokeAgentRuntimeCommand runs shell commands in a session without the model\r\n[HIGH  ] M14-03 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.2)\u001b[m\u001b[K the entrypoint passes the payload's prompt to the framework without checking it is a string: a toolUse block runs a tool with no model in the loop (AgentCore Runtime has no server-side protection for this)\r\n[HIGH  ] M14-04 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.2)\u001b[m\u001b[K the execution role has 10 grants on wildcards (*, memory/*, runtime/*): one compromised session can read other agents' memory, call other runtimes and sandboxes (Unit 42 'Agent God Mode')\r\n[MEDIUM] M14-05 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.2)\u001b[m\u001b[K tsg-agent-runtime-role trust policy has no aws:SourceAccount + aws:SourceArn: any AgentCore resource could assume it (confused deputy)\r\n[MEDIUM] M14-05 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.2)\u001b[m\u001b[K tsg-gateway-role trust policy has no aws:SourceAccount + aws:SourceArn: any AgentCore resource could assume it (confused deputy)\r\n"]
[12.382733, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m14\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m14\u001b[00m$ "]
