[43.216853, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[43.260111, "o", "[HIGH  ] M14-06 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.3)\u001b[m\u001b[K SigV4 runtime and the backend copies runtimeUserId from the browser: AgentCore treats it as an opaque string, so anyone can fetch anyone's tokens from the vault\r\n[HIGH  ] M14-07 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.3)\u001b[m\u001b[K the gateway JWT authorizer checks only allowedScopes: a token issued to ANY app of this identity provider (a partner portal in the same user pool) is accepted\r\n[MEDIUM] M14-08 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.3)\u001b[m\u001b[K nothing explicitly denies GetWorkloadAccessTokenForUserId / InvokeAgentRuntimeForUser: the unverified user-id path stays open\r\n[MEDIUM] M14-09 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.3)\u001b[m\u001b[K 3-legged OAuth without session binding: no registered return URL that checks the signed-in user before CompleteResourceTokenAuth, so a forwarded consent link can bind one user's account to another\r\n[MEDIUM] M14-10 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[K(14.3)\u001b[m\u001b[K GetResourceOauth2Token on '*': the role may use every credential provider in the account; scope it to this workload identity and provider\r\n"]
[43.266235, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m14\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m14\u001b[00m$ "]
